WEBVTT

00:13.967 --> 00:16.377
What are you doing out here?

00:18.557 --> 00:20.887
Listening to the sound of the waves.

00:21.957 --> 00:23.827
You were just listening?

00:24.497 --> 00:25.557
Not looking?

00:26.057 --> 00:27.177
Because...

00:28.227 --> 00:29.727
I can't see them, right?

00:31.627 --> 00:34.687
Then why not come during the day?

00:35.377 --> 00:37.877
I'd rather do that.

00:37.877 --> 00:40.197
But they'd find me if I did.

00:41.157 --> 00:43.697
More importantly, who are you?

00:44.057 --> 00:46.147
I don't think we've met.

00:47.027 --> 00:49.607
I was just brought here recently.

00:49.957 --> 00:52.057
Some stuff happened, you see.

00:52.827 --> 00:54.347
I see.

00:54.347 --> 00:55.957
What's your name?

00:57.617 --> 01:02.007
The grown-ups call me #602.

01:21.807 --> 01:22.787
Nagisa.

01:25.897 --> 01:29.467
Since you love the sea, 
that's what I'll call you.

01:30.917 --> 01:32.697
What's your name?

01:32.697 --> 01:34.607
I don't have a name.

01:35.157 --> 01:36.387
But...

01:36.387 --> 01:37.497
What?

01:38.207 --> 01:40.267
I have a code name, I guess.

03:17.977 --> 03:20.937
EPISODE 1: TO SEE YOU ONCE MORE

03:18.357 --> 03:20.407
Where am I?

03:31.567 --> 03:33.447
What was that for, Natsunagi?

03:33.447 --> 03:35.587
That's my line!

03:35.587 --> 03:38.577
Don't try to kiss your classmate 
when she's asleep!

03:39.437 --> 03:41.067
This isn't fair.

03:41.067 --> 03:44.337
You two are being very loud.

03:44.707 --> 03:46.337
Saikawa?

03:46.767 --> 03:48.587
What are you doing here?

03:49.137 --> 03:53.127
Hmm? You want to know why 
I'm sleeping next to you, Kimizuka-san?

03:53.127 --> 03:55.347
You're asking me?

03:55.347 --> 03:58.417
Why are you saying it like that?

03:58.417 --> 04:00.847
I didn't bring you here, did I?

04:00.847 --> 04:03.607
You really don't remember?

04:03.607 --> 04:04.677
Char?!

04:05.117 --> 04:10.487
We were going to visit Ma'am's grave when 
someone kidnapped us and brought us here.

04:11.237 --> 04:12.507
That's right!

04:12.507 --> 04:14.117
Yes, that's right.

04:14.117 --> 04:18.367
Hmph. You guys are so quick 
to let your guard down.

04:18.367 --> 04:20.497
You were kidnapped too, right?

04:20.497 --> 04:22.627
Jeez! Fine! I'm sorry!

04:34.277 --> 04:39.977
<i>If you're seeing this video, it means...</i>

04:39.977 --> 04:41.847
<i>that Kimizuka Kimihiko,</i>

04:41.847 --> 04:43.477
<i>Natsunagi Nagisa,</i>

04:43.807 --> 04:45.227
<i>Saikawa Yui,</i>

04:45.227 --> 04:47.477
<i>and Charlotte Arisaka Anderson</i>

04:47.477 --> 04:49.807
<i>are all in the room.</i>

04:50.917 --> 04:52.487
Siesta—

04:51.347 --> 04:52.487
Ma'am!

04:52.897 --> 04:55.167
<i>It's been a while, Char.</i>

04:55.167 --> 04:56.467
<i>But I'm sorry.</i>

04:56.467 --> 05:01.747
<i>I recorded this video a year ago, 
knowing this day would come.</i>

05:02.407 --> 05:03.377
Ma'am...

05:04.417 --> 05:07.627
So this is Siesta-san?

05:07.627 --> 05:12.217
<i>Now, there's a reason I brought you all here.</i>

05:12.717 --> 05:15.637
<i>It's about time you learn...</i>

05:15.637 --> 05:18.847
<i>what happened to me a year ago.</i>

05:20.017 --> 05:22.177
What happened?

05:23.687 --> 05:29.457
<i>I want you to see what happened to us...</i>

05:29.457 --> 05:31.527
<i>and the truth of my death.</i>

05:31.807 --> 05:33.777
<i>And then...</i>

05:34.317 --> 05:36.207
<i>I want you to decide.</i>

05:39.117 --> 05:45.167
<i>And thus began a retelling of 
the three years I spent with Siesta.</i>

05:46.777 --> 05:50.667
<i>We met 10,000 meters above the surface 
of the Earth aboard a hijacked airplane</i>

05:50.667 --> 05:53.827
<i>and embarked on a series 
of incredible adventures.</i>

05:54.837 --> 05:58.347
<i>And then, as we battled 
the secret organization SPES,</i>

05:58.347 --> 06:00.457
<i>we met a strange girl named Alicia.</i>

06:00.997 --> 06:05.977
<i>But there was a personality inside her, 
"Hel," that even she didn't know about.</i>

06:06.997 --> 06:09.357
<i>And then we headed to the enemy's hideout,</i>

06:09.877 --> 06:13.527
<i>to follow Hel, or perhaps save Alicia.</i>

06:14.067 --> 06:16.867
<i>There we met Seed, the enemy's leader.</i>

06:17.737 --> 06:21.967
<i>And Siesta began 
her final battle with Hel.</i>

06:23.237 --> 06:26.567
<i>What happened on that island, 
one year ago?</i>

06:26.967 --> 06:29.587
<i>Why is the detective already dead?</i>

06:31.087 --> 06:32.387
<i>They...</i>

06:33.237 --> 06:35.097
<i>She... learned.</i>

06:35.587 --> 06:39.937
<i>The one who took Siesta's life 
on that day, in that place...</i>

06:39.937 --> 06:41.197
It was me.

06:43.977 --> 06:46.317
I killed Siesta-san...

06:47.877 --> 06:51.367
I took the person you cared for most...

06:52.117 --> 06:53.187
I'm sorry.

06:53.507 --> 06:56.047
No, you didn't do anything.

06:56.047 --> 06:57.667
It wasn't you...

06:57.667 --> 06:59.227
It was another...

06:59.947 --> 07:03.157
I didn't just get a heart transplant.

07:03.157 --> 07:06.707
I stole Siesta-san's heart.

07:07.497 --> 07:11.347
And the memories of my youth 
and all that time in the hospital...

07:11.347 --> 07:15.837
were because of the memories 
from that time at SPES...

07:18.427 --> 07:20.947
<i>Natsunagi learned everything.</i>

07:20.947 --> 07:22.477
<i>She remembered.</i>

07:23.217 --> 07:28.837
<i>Alicia and the girl 
called Hel were both her.</i>

07:29.607 --> 07:33.697
You lost your memories 
because of that pollen?

07:33.697 --> 07:36.357
Both Nagisa and Kimizuka were affected?

07:36.657 --> 07:39.907
You remembered the whole time, right, Char?

07:39.907 --> 07:40.737
Yes...

07:40.737 --> 07:42.227
Char-san, I...

07:42.227 --> 07:43.537
Don't say a word.

07:44.297 --> 07:47.457
I know it's not your fault.

07:47.457 --> 07:51.347
But... I still want a little more time.

07:52.677 --> 07:53.477
Right.

07:55.877 --> 07:57.057
Everything's okay.

07:57.057 --> 07:58.127
Let's calm down.

07:59.257 --> 08:00.807
We can clasp our hands.

08:00.807 --> 08:02.137
Rotate our shoulders.

08:02.137 --> 08:03.887
Breathe rhythmically.

08:04.197 --> 08:08.217
Close our eyes, 
take a deep breath in, then out.

08:08.217 --> 08:09.387
Help our blood flow.

08:09.887 --> 08:13.797
Open our eyes, 
and watch our blurry vision clear.

08:15.437 --> 08:16.897
Saikawa...

08:16.897 --> 08:20.817
And when we've done that, 
why don't we all have some tea?

08:21.557 --> 08:22.837
Sheesh...

08:22.837 --> 08:25.407
Why are you the most grown-up of us all?

08:27.877 --> 08:30.467
A tea party? That sounds wonderful.

08:30.467 --> 08:32.787
I hope you'll allow me to join.

08:36.667 --> 08:39.487
The next time you try to touch this body,

08:39.487 --> 08:41.977
I'll shatter every bone in yours.

08:41.977 --> 08:43.547
That's not fair...

08:46.617 --> 08:48.027
You're...

08:50.717 --> 08:52.077
Siesta?

09:02.517 --> 09:05.207
Unfortunately, I don't have any tea cakes.

09:05.207 --> 09:07.627
Shall we have some delivered?

09:07.627 --> 09:09.197
Kimihiko will pay.

09:09.197 --> 09:11.957
Hey, don't be so mean to me.

09:12.407 --> 09:16.077
So, where have we been brought?

09:16.077 --> 09:21.217
This is one of Siesta-sama's hideouts.

09:21.517 --> 09:23.297
First I'm hearing of it...

09:27.317 --> 09:30.277
You really do look just like Ma'am...

09:30.277 --> 09:32.937
Charlotte, I'll say this again.

09:32.937 --> 09:35.007
I'm just a robot.

09:35.427 --> 09:41.227
A bio-android created from a portion 
of Siesta-sama's body, memories,

09:41.227 --> 09:42.947
and abilities before her death.

09:43.387 --> 09:47.407
The name she gave me was "Noches."

09:48.037 --> 09:51.007
It's hard to believe, 
but I guess I have to.

09:51.007 --> 09:55.767
The real one would've let me rest 
on her lap instead of flipping me.

09:56.417 --> 09:59.067
I have queried my database,

09:59.067 --> 10:01.127
and it appears that statement is false.

10:01.127 --> 10:03.027
Don't make it so obvious 
you're looking away.

10:03.027 --> 10:06.297
And if you're modeled on Siesta, 
then stop hating me.

10:06.597 --> 10:11.667
I dislike you <i>because</i> 
I'm modeled on Siesta-sama.

10:11.667 --> 10:14.557
I told you not to be so mean to me.

10:14.557 --> 10:18.847
Why does it sound like the two of them 
have been married for years?

10:18.847 --> 10:21.197
Yui, don't compare them to a couple.

10:21.197 --> 10:22.817
They're more like a veteran comedy duo.

10:23.977 --> 10:25.627
Listen, Noches.

10:25.627 --> 10:28.917
I understand that you're 
the one who kidnapped us.

10:28.917 --> 10:31.447
Which means you needed 
to talk to us, right?

10:34.457 --> 10:39.967
Siesta-sama made many preparations 
before that day.

10:40.467 --> 10:45.587
And I was given the duty 
of telling you the truth.

10:47.837 --> 10:48.907
Nagisa.

10:49.847 --> 10:54.017
It's because of you 
that Siesta-sama's will can be carried on.

10:54.367 --> 10:58.637
Ensuring that you survive 
and attend school

10:58.637 --> 11:02.107
was her last wish 
and the last job she gave me.

11:02.917 --> 11:05.357
So on her behalf, I say...

11:06.917 --> 11:07.967
Thank you.

11:10.457 --> 11:11.967
I...

11:15.537 --> 11:19.747
Why are you telling us about the past now?

11:19.747 --> 11:23.257
Why hide the truth until now?

11:23.257 --> 11:25.307
There are several reasons.

11:25.627 --> 11:29.987
The first being that Siesta-sama 
required a long period of time

11:29.987 --> 11:35.207
to suppress the evil "Hel" personality 
within Nagisa's body

11:35.207 --> 11:37.637
and stabilize Nagisa herself.

11:38.227 --> 11:41.767
And the second reason 
was that she was waiting

11:41.767 --> 11:44.097
for the four of you 
to truly come together.

11:45.477 --> 11:49.157
And the last reason is...

11:49.847 --> 11:51.027
Seed.

11:52.357 --> 11:57.337
Seed has taken no overt actions 
over the course of the last year.

11:57.337 --> 12:02.037
But it seems that's changed recently.

12:02.367 --> 12:06.957
Stopping them is your job, Nagisa.

12:06.957 --> 12:09.047
My job?

12:09.387 --> 12:12.047
It's not just Natsunagi's problem, right?

12:12.507 --> 12:14.037
That is correct.

12:14.487 --> 12:21.437
But her role is far greater 
than yours, Yui's, or Charlotte's.

12:21.897 --> 12:25.817
Because Nagisa is the Great Detective.

12:27.567 --> 12:31.977
That's right. 
Siesta-sama didn't tell you yet.

12:32.517 --> 12:34.697
Our "Great Detective" is—

12:34.697 --> 12:35.697
Wait!

12:36.037 --> 12:40.327
Another word and you'll violate 
the Federation Charter!

12:40.707 --> 12:42.077
I don't care.

12:42.417 --> 12:45.647
They're a part of this, too.

12:50.177 --> 12:54.887
The Great Detective is one of the Tuners,

12:54.887 --> 12:57.267
the twelve shields 
that protect this world.

12:57.637 --> 12:59.017
"Tuners"?

12:59.017 --> 13:02.217
There are dangers that arise 
throughout the world at regular intervals,

13:02.217 --> 13:04.517
many at the same time...

13:05.137 --> 13:07.067
And an international organization

13:07.067 --> 13:10.727
has secretly drafted in individuals
 to deal with them.

13:11.197 --> 13:13.067
The "Tuners."

13:13.817 --> 13:16.177
There are 12 in all.

13:16.177 --> 13:17.977
They all have different roles.

13:17.977 --> 13:20.887
The "Phantom Thief," 
"the Shrine Maiden," the "Assassin."

13:20.887 --> 13:25.167
It's said that one of them 
is even a vampire.

13:25.427 --> 13:27.017
A vampire?

13:27.017 --> 13:31.417
But a year ago, Siesta-sama passed away,

13:31.907 --> 13:34.257
and the role of the "Great Detective"

13:34.257 --> 13:37.427
whose job it is to destroy SPES 
became vacant.

13:37.867 --> 13:44.387
It's likely that you, Nagisa, will be 
designated the next Great Detective.

13:45.107 --> 13:47.957
Of course, it hasn't been decided yet.

13:47.957 --> 13:51.577
But you have the heart of 
the previous Great Detective,

13:51.577 --> 13:53.817
and you carry on her will.

13:53.817 --> 13:58.887
And you can master powers 
beyond those of a normal human.

13:59.477 --> 14:04.077
Many people will think that 
sufficient reason.

14:04.367 --> 14:07.867
Siesta won't appear 
inside her body anymore.

14:07.867 --> 14:09.337
I know.

14:09.727 --> 14:13.727
And so I ask you once more, on her behalf.

14:14.407 --> 14:19.507
Nagisa, will you truly carry on 
the will of the Great Detective?

14:20.557 --> 14:22.017
I...

14:22.637 --> 14:27.637
If... just hypothetically, 
she were to say yes,

14:27.637 --> 14:29.287
what should she do first?

14:30.457 --> 14:31.717
Hmm...

14:34.997 --> 14:38.237
Let's have her hunt for a mistake.

14:42.297 --> 14:46.687
<i>If Natsunagi is unsure about 
becoming the Great Detective,</i>

14:47.097 --> 14:52.497
<i>she can first find a "mistake" in that 
footage from a year ago she saw yesterday</i>

14:52.497 --> 14:54.507
<i>and decide then.</i>

14:56.007 --> 14:58.187
<i>That's what Noches said.</i>

14:56.437 --> 14:58.377
Wow, what's with that reaction?

14:58.377 --> 14:59.507
What's going on?

14:58.957 --> 15:00.827
<i>And then she let us go.</i>

15:04.557 --> 15:08.267
But we don't have any clues...

15:19.107 --> 15:20.327
You're kidding me.

15:21.637 --> 15:25.967
You ate lunch all alone, and then 
you've been sleeping here ever since?

15:26.457 --> 15:29.137
Lunch tastes better on the roof.

15:29.137 --> 15:31.207
That's not the point.

15:31.487 --> 15:35.217
You would've been spending the night at 
school if I hadn't come to get you, right?

15:35.657 --> 15:37.637
Why not make some friends?

15:37.637 --> 15:39.947
It's not that I don't make friends.

15:39.947 --> 15:41.327
It's that I <i>can't</i>.

15:43.037 --> 15:46.297
Well, you can count me, if you want.

15:46.297 --> 15:48.867
On your "friend counter."

15:48.867 --> 15:52.547
Isn't it nice to have somebody 
you can talk to about anything?

15:52.547 --> 15:53.777
And she's cute, too!

15:55.497 --> 15:58.487
I've never had a friend, 
so I wouldn't know.

15:58.487 --> 16:00.367
You're such a contrarian.

16:00.367 --> 16:03.277
I don't know how you 
got along with Siesta-san.

16:03.697 --> 16:06.287
We never really did get along.

16:06.287 --> 16:08.827
We would have a fight 
at least  every three days.

16:08.827 --> 16:12.037
Would you be the first 
to apologize when it happened?

16:12.037 --> 16:14.117
Most of the time.

16:14.117 --> 16:18.047
But sometimes, I'd get stubborn 
and not talk to her for a week.

16:18.387 --> 16:19.627
And then?

16:19.907 --> 16:22.307
She'd start to freak out.

16:22.307 --> 16:24.347
Siesta-san's that cute?

16:24.627 --> 16:27.327
And then when I'd go to talk to her again,

16:27.327 --> 16:30.727
she'd look relieved 
for a single instant, and then...

16:31.057 --> 16:34.897
She'd go back to looking upset 
and say, "Are you stupid?"

16:34.897 --> 16:36.547
Yup, that's right.

16:36.547 --> 16:37.407
Good work.

16:37.407 --> 16:39.807
You'd get an A grade in Siesta-isms.

16:41.477 --> 16:46.617
You know, you look happy 
when you talk about her.

16:48.037 --> 16:52.417
She was all you really wanted, wasn't she?

16:53.747 --> 16:54.947
Don't worry about it.

16:55.477 --> 16:58.417
I was alone before I met her, too.

16:59.647 --> 17:02.177
You're a nice guy.

17:03.107 --> 17:05.427
But it's no good.

17:05.837 --> 17:08.517
Even when I'm talking 
to my friends in class,

17:08.517 --> 17:10.937
or when you're trying to cheer me up,

17:11.267 --> 17:14.647
I can't get the sight of it 
out of my head.

17:14.947 --> 17:17.977
And it's not just Siesta-san.

17:18.507 --> 17:23.037
I've hurt so many other innocent 
people with my own hands...

17:18.507 --> 17:21.657
Sorry to keep you waiting. Huh? Where's Nagi?

17:21.657 --> 17:24.117
She said to leave without her.

17:31.997 --> 17:32.907
So gloomy.

17:33.207 --> 17:34.957
Wh-Wh-Wh-Wh-Wh-What?

17:36.247 --> 17:37.707
Listen to me, Natsunagi.

17:37.707 --> 17:40.467
It's still my turn to be angry.

17:40.467 --> 17:43.137
Huh? This isn't your kink?

17:43.587 --> 17:46.807
I-I-I-I'll kill you twice!

17:48.197 --> 17:49.367
A long time ago...

17:50.267 --> 17:54.477
When I was really down and depressed...

17:54.867 --> 17:57.177
Siesta slapped me on the back.

17:58.087 --> 18:01.607
So I'll always be there 
to slap you on the back, too,

18:02.087 --> 18:03.857
and hold your hand.

18:05.627 --> 18:09.117
All you did was run your fingertip 
down my back.

18:09.917 --> 18:12.187
You can get as depressed 
as you want right now.

18:12.847 --> 18:16.527
You can order takeout 
and stress eat as much as you want.

18:16.527 --> 18:20.587
Or curse the unfairness of it all using 
as much foul language as you want.

18:21.197 --> 18:24.507
If that still won't wash away your guilt,

18:24.507 --> 18:26.217
then I'll carry half of it.

18:26.637 --> 18:29.837
I couldn't save her then, either.

18:30.467 --> 18:35.977
So the least I can do 
is carry some of your pain.

18:36.827 --> 18:38.057
Kimizuka...

18:38.897 --> 18:41.227
Well, uh, you know...

18:41.547 --> 18:45.167
I feel like once I say this, 
I'll never escape it, but...

18:46.147 --> 18:48.987
I'm used to girls being mean to me!

18:53.907 --> 18:57.747
What? Why are you
sharing your fetish now?

18:58.287 --> 19:01.197
Hey, I'm trying to make you feel better!

19:01.197 --> 19:04.577
You're cheering me up by confessing 
that you're a masochist?

19:04.577 --> 19:05.687
That's crazy.

19:05.687 --> 19:08.007
You're more messed up than I thought!

19:08.567 --> 19:10.537
I was kidding...

19:10.537 --> 19:12.977
I just wanted to make you laugh...

19:12.977 --> 19:15.477
It's not actually my fetish...

19:19.147 --> 19:20.667
You're so dumb.

19:22.617 --> 19:24.677
You really are so dumb.

19:26.837 --> 19:28.487
Which of us is?

19:31.597 --> 19:33.697
You've been holding it in for so long.

19:51.127 --> 19:54.067
Now that you've stopped crying,

19:54.067 --> 19:57.347
let's start talking about that "mistake" 
Noches was referring to.

19:57.717 --> 20:00.357
Do you have any ideas?

20:00.357 --> 20:02.287
No, none.

20:02.947 --> 20:09.667
When Siesta was alive, 
she said that "past" was the truth.

20:09.667 --> 20:12.867
But something in it was wrong.

20:13.267 --> 20:18.497
Which means that when she was alive, 
Siesta made a mistake, maybe?

20:18.497 --> 20:22.997
But would Siesta-san make a mistake?

20:22.997 --> 20:24.547
True...

20:24.547 --> 20:29.127
Maybe it's fastest to talk 
to the people involved?

20:29.657 --> 20:34.257
There's me and Siesta, then you. Who else?

20:34.257 --> 20:40.557
Char... But if she didn't say anything then,
 nothing must've occurred to her.

20:40.557 --> 20:42.267
Maybe our enemies, then?

20:42.267 --> 20:44.127
SPES, huh?

20:44.127 --> 20:47.277
But then how would we talk to them?

20:53.367 --> 20:54.277
Hel.

20:55.657 --> 20:59.907
But Siesta sealed Hel away inside me, right?

20:59.907 --> 21:01.607
We're going to call her out?

21:02.197 --> 21:04.727
But then she'll have 
sealed her away for nothing—

21:04.727 --> 21:05.457
One year.

21:07.517 --> 21:10.377
She spent one year persuading her.

21:10.977 --> 21:12.677
I'm sure it'll be okay.

21:13.447 --> 21:16.177
But her...

21:16.497 --> 21:18.307
I heard what you were saying.

21:19.297 --> 21:20.807
If you're going to summon Hel,

21:21.107 --> 21:22.987
please leave it to me.

21:24.787 --> 21:27.357
So? Why are we in my house?

21:27.357 --> 21:32.067
This was the closest place where it 
seemed safe to make a lot of noise.

21:32.067 --> 21:35.447
I didn't say anything about it 
being okay to make a lot of noise...

21:37.487 --> 21:42.517
Is it okay for a detective to ask 
for help from a client, anyway?

21:42.517 --> 21:45.317
You really are an idiot, Kimihiko.

21:45.707 --> 21:48.207
Siesta-sama would have said

21:48.717 --> 21:52.967
that it's okay to do anything to 
protect your client's interests.

21:54.117 --> 21:56.277
You're right.

21:58.627 --> 22:00.217
Noches-san.

22:00.507 --> 22:05.327
How can I meet Hel... the other me?

22:09.627 --> 22:12.857
We'll summon her into that mirror.

22:16.167 --> 22:17.117
Hold this.

22:17.517 --> 22:21.287
And then stare at yourself in the mirror.

22:21.287 --> 22:22.907
Mirrors facing each other?

22:22.907 --> 22:26.167
There are sayings about
mirrors facing each other.

22:26.167 --> 22:29.707
They say a pair of mirrors 
can summon a devil.

22:29.707 --> 22:33.167
That they can show 
the past and the future.

22:34.207 --> 22:36.047
It's not difficult.

22:36.377 --> 22:42.057
If you wish to see her, the slightest 
chance will bring Hel to you.

22:42.557 --> 22:47.807
So just keep looking 
at yourself in the mirror.

23:20.387 --> 23:21.717
Natsunagi?

23:24.627 --> 23:26.227
It's been a long time.

23:32.327 --> 23:34.087
Master.

23:34.987 --> 23:39.987
EPISODE 2: 
A STORY OF THAT DAY NO ONE KNOWS
